quran[17]{c,v,t}:
  23,1,"Indeed, the believers have prospered."
  23,2,"Those who are humble in their prayers,"
  23,3,"who turn away from idle talk,"
  23,4,"who give the alms (i.e. mandatory charity),"
  23,5,"who guard their private parts (protecting their chastity),"
  23,6,"except with their wives or whom their right hands possess (i.e. the female captives in their lawful custody), for then they are not blameworthy;"
  23,7,"but whoever seeks beyond that, they are the transgressors;"
  23,8,"and those who keep their trusts and their pledges,"
  23,9,"and who are (persistently) observant of their prayers,"
  23,10,these are the ones who will be the heirs;
  23,11,"who shall inherit Paradise, abiding therein forever."
  23,12,"Indeed, We created human being from an extract (i.e. the chemical ingredients) of clay.*"
  23,13,"Then, We placed him as a fertilised egg (i.e. a zygote*) in a secure abode (of the mother’s womb)."
  23,14,"Then We made that zygote a clinging mass.* Then We developed that clinging mass into a lump of flesh (chewed with teeth). Then, out of this chewed lump, We developed a structure of bones and clothed the bones with flesh (and muscle). Later, We developed it (gradually) into a new form. So blessed is Allah, the Best of creators."
  23,15,"Then, after that, you will surely die."
  23,16,Then you will indeed be raised on the Day of Resurrection.
  23,17,"And certainly, We have created above you seven tracks.* And We have never been heedless of (Our) creation."
